All cells for substrings of length 2 are empty. This is a critical point. In the CYK algorithm, larger substrings are formed by combining smaller substrings. If no non-terminals can be derived from any substring of length 2, then it's impossible to derive any non-terminals for substrings of length 3, 4, and so on, up to the full string length.

