**Length l = 3 to 9:**
For each subsequent length `l` and starting position `i`, we iterate through all possible split points `k` (from 1 to `l-1`). We check combinations of non-terminals from P[k][i] and P[l-k][i+k]. If any combination (A, B) forms a rule C -> A B, we add C to P[l][i].

During this process, it becomes apparent that the table remains largely empty. The only non-empty cell found so far is P[2][5] = {NT51}.

Let's continue to fill the table. For any cell P[l][i], if either P[k][i] or P[l-k][i+k] is empty for all `k`, then P[l][i] will also be empty. Since almost all cells for length 2 are empty, it propagates to longer lengths.

