This pattern continues. None of the non-empty cells can combine to form other non-terminals as there are no matching production rules. As a result, all cells in the CYK table for lengths greater than 2, including the final cell P[9][0], will remain empty.

Since P[9][0] does not contain the starting non-terminal 'S', the string `t81 t98 t24 t19 t75 t35 t19 t54 t80` cannot be generated by the given grammar.

